endobj

142 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(When you apply for a job, your CV doesn\220t go straight to a recruiter. It goes through an ATS, a robot that filters out applications before a human even gets to see them. Why? Because of the sheer volume.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

143 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Every single job post here gets between 2,000 to 4,000 applications. And recruiters are often hiring for multiple roles at once. That means 10,000 to 20,000 CVs to filter through. It\220s impossible to do it manually.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

144 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(So the ATS scans your CV for structure, keywords, and clarity. Not creativity, not beauty, just data. It\220s harsh, but that\220s how it works.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

