407 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(How to work with recruitment agencies the smart way)/E(How to work with recruitment agencies the smart way)/Pg 27 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

408 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Now that you know who to contact, here\220s how to do it without wasting your time or theirs.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

409 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(1. Only contact agencies that work in your field.)/E(1. Only contact agencies that work in your field.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

410 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Read their website. Check the jobs they post. Look at their LinkedIn. If they haven\220t posted anything in your industry for months, move on. Some agencies focus only on tech. Some only hire for senior roles. Some cover multiple industries. You need to find the ones that match your background and your goals.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

411 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(2. Don\220t send just your CV.)/E(2. Don\220t send just your CV.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

412 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Always include a short message. Say what kind of role you\220re looking for, how many years of experience you have, and what kinds of companies you\220ve worked with. Be clear about your industry experience too. If you\220ve worked in events, hospitality, fintech, education, or anything else, say it. That gives the recruiter context and helps them understand where you fit.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

413 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(3. Be specific.)/E(3. Be specific.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

414 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Say something like, "I\220m looking for a mid-level HR role in the events or hospitality industry in Dubai. I have 5.5 years of experience in HR roles within the events space and another 2.5 years in hospitality. I also have a strong network of HR professionals and freelancers in these industries, which really helps when it comes to recruitment, onboarding, and referrals.")/Pg 27 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

415 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(That\220s the kind of message that gets noticed. Not \215I\220m open to anything in HR.\216 The more specific you are, the easier it is for the recruiter to actually imagine you in a role they\220re hiring for.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

416 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(4. Don\220t ghost them and don\220t chase them.)/E(4. Don\220t ghost them and don\220t chase them.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

417 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(If they reply, great. Be responsive and respectful. If they don\220t, it usually means they don\220t have something right now. You can follow up once or twice, but not every two days. Nobody likes pressure. Stay professional.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

418 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(5. Keep them updated.)/E(5. Keep them updated.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

419 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E( If you move cities, change industries, or shift your job title, tell them. If you see a role they post and it fits you, apply and message them directly with why you\220re a match. Recruiters appreciate people who stay visible and relevant.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

420 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 83 0 R/T(6. Track who you messaged.)/E(6. Track who you messaged.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

421 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Use a simple Google Sheet. Note the agency name, recruiter name, date contacted, what you said, and any replies. This keeps you from repeating yourself or forgetting who you already reached out to. It shows you\220re organised and most people are not.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

422 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 84 0 R/T(Events in the UAE that actually matter)/E(Events in the UAE that actually matter)/Pg 28 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

423 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Here\220s something a lot of job seekers don\220t want to hear but need to.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

424 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(If you\220re only applying online and never showing up in real life, you\220re missing out on jobs that never get posted. In the UAE, networking is everything. The job market here is fast, personal, and full of last-minute openings that go to people someone already knows. That means attending events isn\220t just a nice extra. It\220s part of the job search. It\220s where you shake hands with the right people, hear what roles are coming soon, and get remembered.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

425 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(And I don\220t mean going to expos just to collect flyers. You need to show up prepared. You need to speak to people. You need to follow up. That\220s where the real magic happens.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

426 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 84 0 R/T(What kind of events should you attend?)/E(What kind of events should you attend?)/Pg 28 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

427 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(It depends on your industry, but here\220s a simple rule: If your industry is gathering, you should be there.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

428 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Whether it\220s a tech summit, HR breakfast, fashion trade show, or startup pitch night if those are your people, go meet them.)/Pg 28 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

429 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 84 0 R/T(Real networking happens offline too)/E(Real networking happens offline too)/Pg 28 0 R/K[7]>>
